<article class="env-lemma" id="0116">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0116">Lemma <span data-tag="0116">12.13.11</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If the maps $f, g : A^\bullet \to B^\bullet $ are homotopic, then the induced maps $H^ i(f)$ and $H^ i(g)$ are equal. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $f : A^\bullet \to B^\bullet $ is a homotopy equivalence, then $f$ is a quasi-isomorphism. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
